<stack-static>
    <statement><p><p>An aircraft flies due east along the parallel <m>32^\circ\,\mathrm{N}</m> from <m>5^\circ\,\mathrm{E}</m> to <m>40^\circ\,\mathrm{E}</m> at <m>{420}</m> knots.</p><p>(a) Find the distance it flies, to the nearest nautical mile.</p><p><fillin characters="8" name="ans1"/> nm  </p><p>(b) Find the time it takes, to the nearest minute.</p><p><fillin characters="3" name="ans2"/> h <fillin characters="3" name="ans3"/> min   </p></p></statement>
    <solution><p><p>(a) The difference in longitude is <m>{35}^\circ = {2100}'</m>. Along a parallel, multiply by <m>\cos(\text{latitude})</m>:</p><p><me>{2100} \times \cos {32}^\circ = {1780.9} \approx {1781} \text{ nm}.</me></p><p>(b) Time <m>=</m> distance <m>\div</m> speed <m>= {1780.9} \div {420} = {4.240}</m> h. The decimal part is a fraction of an hour: <m>{0.240} \times 60 = {14.4}</m> min. So the flight takes <m>{4}</m> h <m>{14}</m> min.</p></p></solution>
    <answer><p><m>1780.90100193</m></p></answer>
    <answer><p><m>4</m></p></answer>
    <answer><p><m>14</m></p></answer>
</stack-static>